      "text": "Let's break down the problem step-by-step.\n\n1. We are given that the pressure \\(P\\) of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume \\(V\\). This can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}\n   \\]\n   or\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{k}{V}\n   \\]\n   where \\(k\\) is a constant.\n\n2. We start with a certain amount of oxygen in a 2.28 liter container with a pressure of 5 kPa. Let's find the constant \\(k\\) using the initial conditions:\n   \\[\n   5 = \\frac{k}{2.28}\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(k\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   k = 5 \\times 2.28 = 11.4\n   \\]\n\n3. Now, we have 11.4 kPa of oxygen in a 5.7 liter container. Let \\(P_{\\text{new}}\\) be the new pressure in the 5.7 liter container. Using the formula for inverse proportionality again, we have:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{new}} = \\frac{11.4}{5.7}\n   \\]\n   Calculating this, we get:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{new}} \\approx 2 \\text{ kPa}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the new pressure will be \\(\\boxed{2}\\) kPa.",
