      "text": "To find the new pressure of the oxygen in the 5.7 liter container, we start by analyzing the inverse proportionality between pressure and volume under constant temperature. Given our initial conditions,\n- Let p₁ be the initial pressure = 5 kPa\n- Let V₁ be the initial volume = 2.28 liters\n- Let p₂ be the unknown final pressure (which we want to find)\n\nBy the principle of inverse proportionality in the formula R/T = K, where R and T are constants, and K is the product of the ratio of pressure (p₁/p₂) and volume (V₁/V₂), we get:\n\nK = (p₁ * V₁) / (p₂ * V₂)\n\nSubstituting the known values:\nK = (5 kPa * 2.28 liters) / (p₂ * 5.7 liters)\n\nSince the pressure remains constant under the same conditions, the product of the pressure and volume stays the same from initial to final states:\np₁ * V₁ = p₂ * V₂.\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n5 kPa * 2.28 liters = p₂ * 5.7 liters.\n\nSolving for p₂:\np₂ = (5 kPa * 2.28 liters) / 5.7 liters\n   = 11.4 kPa / 5.7\n\nLet's compute the value:\np₂ = 2 kPa\n\nSo, the new pressure in Kpa would be 2 kPa.",
